    {
      "title": "Finding backup heads and their triggers",
      "summary": "Comparing models with their main heads present and removed helps locate backup heads across model families. Targeted interventions reveal query signals beyond the unembedding direction—the direction used to read out an output score—and limited relief from replacing activations in heads that suppress output.",
